1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:07,124
At seven a.m. sharp, the woman across the street opened her window... and said four words.

2
00:00:07,574 --> 00:00:09,352
That should be impossible.

3
00:00:10,002 --> 00:00:15,110
Because in this town, every person gets three words a day. Not one more.

4
00:00:15,860 --> 00:00:17,950
The baker spends his on bread.

5
00:00:18,100 --> 00:00:22,642
And after the third word... nothing. Silence, until midnight.

6
00:00:23,392 --> 00:00:25,761
So where did her fourth word come from?

7
00:00:31,711 --> 00:00:35,657
He had lived across from her for years, and never said a thing.

8
00:00:35,907 --> 00:00:40,366
Every morning he watched her window. She never once looked his way.

9
00:00:40,616 --> 00:00:43,087
Not because he had nothing to say.

10
00:00:43,237 --> 00:00:45,661
Because three words were never enough.

11
00:00:46,411 --> 00:00:50,017
So he made a plan. Stop talking. Save every word.

12
00:00:50,167 --> 00:00:52,254
And one day, tell her everything.

13
00:00:53,704 --> 00:01:00,273
Every midnight, his three unspoken words dropped into a jar. He kept the lid shut tight.

14
00:01:01,923 --> 00:01:03,988
Day one. Three words saved.

15
00:01:06,123 --> 00:01:11,899
Day nine. The baker asked how he was. He just smiled, and pointed at the bread.

16
00:01:14,149 --> 00:01:17,759
That morning, across the street, she said five words.

17
00:01:19,209 --> 00:01:24,624
Day sixty. A hundred and eighty words. He practiced his speech every night.

18
00:01:26,074 --> 00:01:29,951
And she had started singing. Whole songs, every morning.

19
00:01:31,401 --> 00:01:37,572
Day two hundred. His phone stopped ringing. Nobody calls a man who never answers.

20
00:01:39,022 --> 00:01:45,401
Day three hundred sixty-four. One thousand and ninety-two words. Enough for everything.

21
00:01:48,051 --> 00:01:49,935
That night, he couldn't sleep.

22
00:01:50,285 --> 00:01:53,854
At midnight, three more words dropped into the jar...

23
00:01:54,104 --> 00:01:56,902
and then, slowly... they slipped back out.

24
00:01:57,252 --> 00:02:00,507
Through the lid. Through the window. Across the street.

25
00:02:00,657 --> 00:02:02,219
Straight into hers.

26
00:02:03,069 --> 00:02:06,205
He tore off the lid. The jar was empty.

27
00:02:06,555 --> 00:02:08,534
It had been empty all year.

28
00:02:09,184 --> 00:02:13,210
Every word he never said had gone to her. Every single night.

29
00:02:13,860 --> 00:02:17,971
That fourth word, on the very first morning? It was his.

30
00:02:19,521 --> 00:02:24,735
At seven a.m., her window opened. And this time, she looked straight at him.

31
00:02:25,085 --> 00:02:27,375
She used all three of her words.

32
00:02:29,185 --> 00:02:32,963
Now it was his turn. He had exactly three words...

33
00:02:33,313 --> 00:02:35,054
and a whole year to say.
